    <!-- Section 1: Exporting to GitHub -->
    <div class="yt-card p-4 mb-4 border-start border-4 border-dark">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-3">
            <i class="bi bi-github fs-3 text-dark"></i>
            <div>
                <h4 class="fw-bold mb-0">Part 1: How to Export this Project to a New GitHub Repository</h4>
                <small class="text-muted">Two easy options: 1-Click UI Export or Terminal Git Push</small>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row g-4 mt-1">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="p-3 border rounded-3 bg-white h-100 shadow-sm">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="badge bg-danger rounded-circle p-2 px-3 fw-bold">Option A</span>
                        <h6 class="fw-bold mb-0 text-dark">1-Click Export via AI Studio Menu (Recommended)</h6>
                    </div>
                    <ol class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-3">
                        <li class="mb-2">Look at the <strong>top-right header of Google AI Studio</strong> (next to the Share/Settings menu).</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Click <strong>Settings &rarr; Export to GitHub</strong> (or <strong>Download as ZIP</strong>).</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Sign in to your GitHub account and authorize Google AI Studio.</li>
                        <li class="mb-2">Name your new repository (e.g., <code>youtube-shorts-automation-studio</code>) and click <strong>Create Repository</strong>.</li>
                        <li>AI Studio will automatically push all clean source files, schemas, and configurations directly to your GitHub account!</li>
                    </ol>
                    <div class="p-2 bg-success bg-opacity-10 text-success rounded border border-success small">
                        <i class="bi bi-check-circle-fill me-1"></i> Instant sync &mdash; no terminal or command-line setup needed.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="p-3 border rounded-3 bg-white h-100 shadow-sm">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="badge bg-dark rounded-circle p-2 px-3 fw-bold">Option B</span>
                        <h6 class="fw-bold mb-0 text-dark">Manual Git Push via Terminal / CLI</h6>
                    </div>
                    <p class="small text-muted mb-2">
                        If you have downloaded the code or are working in a local terminal:
                    </p>
                    <div class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded font-monospace small mb-2 overflow-x-auto">
                        <div class="text-secondary"># 1. Create a new empty repo on github.com/new</div>
                        <div class="text-secondary"># 2. In your project directory:</div>
                        git init<br>
                        git add .<br>
                        git commit -m "feat: initial YouTube automation studio"<br>
                        git branch -M main<br>
                        git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USER/YOUR_REPO.git<br>
                        git push -u origin main
                    </div>
                    <small class="text-muted"><i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i> A clean <code>.gitignore</code> and <code>vercel.json</code> are already generated in the root directory.</small>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: Deployment Comparison (Vercel vs Cloud Run vs Render) -->
    <div class="yt-card p-4 mb-4">
        <h4 class="fw-bold mb-3"><i class="bi bi-cloud-upload-fill text-danger me-2"></i>Part 2: Real-World Deployment &mdash; Vercel vs. 24/7 Always-On</h4>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-4">
            You asked if <strong>Vercel</strong> is better. Here is the honest industry comparison for this specific type of app:
        </p>

        <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
            <!-- Vercel -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="p-3 border rounded-3 bg-light h-100 position-relative">
                    <span class="badge bg-dark position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-3">Serverless</span>
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-triangle-fill text-dark me-1"></i> Deploy on Vercel</h5>
                    <small class="text-muted d-block mb-3">Great for web dashboard UI &amp; analytics</small>
                    
                    <ul class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Free SSL, global CDN, instant GitHub sync on git push, zero cost.</li>
                        <li><strong>Caveat:</strong> Vercel runs <em>Serverless Functions</em> (spins down after 10-60 seconds). Background 24/7 cron loops sleep when no one is visiting.</li>
                        <li><strong>Verdict:</strong> Excellent for analyzing channels, previewing viral clips, and triggering posts manually. For 24/7 auto-posting while you sleep, pair with an external free ping (e.g. Cron-Job.org).</li>
                    </ul>

                    <a href="#vercel-steps" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm w-100 fw-bold">View Vercel Steps Below &darr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Cloud Run -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="p-3 border border-success rounded-3 bg-white h-100 position-relative shadow-sm">
                    <span class="badge bg-success position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-3">100% Free &bull; Best Option</span>
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-1 text-success"><i class="bi bi-google me-1"></i> Google Cloud Run</h5>
                    <small class="text-muted d-block mb-3">Native 24/7 container deployment</small>
                    
                    <ul class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Pros:</strong> 1-Click native deploy right in Google AI Studio! Generous <strong>2M requests/month free</strong> forever.</li>
                        <li><strong>Uptime:</strong> Native Node.js Express runtime with zero function timeouts. Full WebSocket &amp; streaming support.</li>
                        <li><strong>Verdict:</strong> <strong>Top recommendation.</strong> Runs the entire engine 24/7 with zero configuration and zero bills.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <a href="#cloudrun-steps" class="btn btn-success btn-sm w-100 fw-bold">View Cloud Run Steps Below &darr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Render / Railway -->
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="p-3 border rounded-3 bg-light h-100 position-relative">
                    <span class="badge bg-primary position-absolute top-0 end-0 m-3">GitHub Web Service</span>
                    <h5 class="fw-bold mb-1"><i class="bi bi-hdd-network-fill text-primary me-1"></i> Render / Railway</h5>
                    <small class="text-muted d-block mb-3">Always-on Node.js background worker</small>
                    
                    <ul class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-3">
                        <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Connects directly to your GitHub repo, auto-deploys on every git push, keeps <code>server.js</code> running continuously.</li>
                        <li><strong>Free Tier:</strong> Render offers 750 free instance hours/month (enough for 1 full web service).</li>
                        <li><strong>Verdict:</strong> Great alternative if you want a standalone Git-connected container server.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <a href="#render-steps" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm w-100 fw-bold">View Render Steps Below &darr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Step by Step Vercel Walkthrough -->
        <div id="vercel-steps" class="p-4 bg-light rounded-3 border mb-4">
            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-3"><i class="bi bi-triangle-fill text-dark me-2"></i>How to Deploy to Vercel Step-by-Step:</h5>
            <ol class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-3">
                <li class="mb-2"><strong>Push your repo to GitHub:</strong> Complete Part 1 above so your code is on GitHub. (We have already configured <code>vercel.json</code> and <code>api/index.js</code> for you).</li>
                <li class="mb-2">Go to <a href="https://vercel.com/new" target="_blank" class="fw-bold text-dark">vercel.com/new</a> and sign in with your GitHub account.</li>
                <li class="mb-2">Click <strong>Import</strong> next to your repository (e.g. <code>youtube-shorts-automation-studio</code>).</li>
                <li class="mb-2">
                    Under <strong>Environment Variables</strong>, add:
                    <ul class="font-monospace text-dark mt-1">
                        <li><code>SESSION_SECRET</code> = <code>super_secure_random_key_2026</code></li>
                        <li><code>YOUTUBE_API_KEY</code> = [Your YouTube Data API v3 key from Google Cloud Console]</li>
                        <li><code>GEMINI_API_KEY</code> = [Optional, for AI video concept generation]</li>
                    </ul>
                </li>
                <li class="mb-2">Click <strong>Deploy</strong>. Within 45 seconds, Vercel will give you a live production URL like <code>https://your-app.vercel.app</code>!</li>
                <li><strong>Pro-Tip for 24/7 Scheduled Automation:</strong> On Vercel, set up a free account on <a href="https://cron-job.org" target="_blank" class="text-primary fw-bold">cron-job.org</a> to ping <code>https://your-app.vercel.app/schedule</code> every 10 minutes to trigger automated checks without sleeping.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- Step by Step Cloud Run Walkthrough -->
        <div id="cloudrun-steps" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-3 border border-success mb-4 shadow-sm">
            <h5 class="fw-bold text-success mb-3"><i class="bi bi-google me-2"></i>How to Deploy to Google Cloud Run (1-Click &amp; 100% Free):</h5>
            <ol class="small text-muted ps-3 mb-0">
                <li class="mb-2">In the <strong>Google AI Studio Build top header</strong>, click the blue <strong>Deploy</strong> button.</li>
                <li class="mb-2">Select your Google Cloud Project (or let AI Studio create the standard free tier project).</li>
                <li class="mb-2">Under <strong>Environment Variables</strong>, confirm <code>PORT=3000</code> and your <code>SESSION_SECRET</code> are set.</li>
                <li class="mb-2">Click <strong>Confirm &amp; Deploy</strong>. Cloud Run compiles the container and issues a permanent, public SSL URL: <code>https://your-service.run.app</code>.</li>
                <li>Your app is live 24/7 worldwide with zero maintenance and zero server fees!</li>
            </ol>
        </div>
    </div>

